// Universal Chess -- re-evaluate BLE advertising after any apt/dpkg run.
//
// A kernel or bluez update can break "Add Extended Advertising Data" (kernel
// 6.18 length validation vs the released-BlueZ sizeof bug), or a later update
// can ship the fix and make our patch unnecessary. After apt finishes, kick the
// self-heal unit to re-check and apply/retire the patched bluetoothd as needed.
//
// --no-block returns immediately so this never deadlocks apt against itself; the
// unit runs after apt exits, takes the dpkg lock with its own timeout, and is a
// fast no-op when bluez + kernel are unchanged since the last successful run.
DPkg::Post-Invoke {
    "if [ -x /usr/bin/systemctl ]; then systemctl start --no-block universal-chess-bluez-selfheal.service || true; fi";
};
